body:
I haven't read through the PR yet but brief overview:

### properties
I haven't read through the PR, but `fti_update_servers_property()` is strictly optional. It exists to allow interpolation for things that aren't directly part of the node transform (the regular xform is normally handled for you as part of `Node3D`).

Unless you are specifically adding FTI support for something in your class, there is no strict need to add the property stubs to a class (and indeed it can cause problems if you don't call the parent).

Here's the description in `Node3D`:
```
	// Opportunity after FTI to update the servers
	// with global_transform_interpolated,
	// and any custom interpolated data in derived classes.
	// Make sure to call the parent class fti_update_servers(),
	// so all data is updated to the servers.
	virtual void fti_update_servers_xform() {}
	virtual void fti_update_servers_property() {}

	// Pump the FTI data, also gives a chance for inherited classes
	// to pump custom data, but they *must* call the base class here too.
	// This is the opportunity for classes to move current values for
	// transforms and properties to stored previous values,
	// and this should take place both on ticks, and during resets.
	virtual void fti_pump_xform();
	virtual void fti_pump_property() {}
```

The reason the property stubs are used in `Camera3D` specifically is we added  the ability to interpolate `fov`, `size`, `frustum_offset`, `near` and `far` properties in that class.

So TLDR, if `XRCamera` is just inheriting those properties from `Camera3D`, you shouldn't need a stub in there for `fti_update_servers_property()`.

Note that *because* there is a stub in this PR, and it is *not* calling the parent `fti_update_servers_property`, this will be breaking the XR cameras inherited `Camera3D` property interpolation. Unless that is required / desired, that may be a bug, so I would recommend just removing the `fti_update_servers_property()` function completely, and relying on the inherited `Camera3D` or `Node3D` version (for now) unless it is added for specific reason.

_(I'm happy to help fixup any specifics for the XR Camera as a follow up if you need any properties interpolated for example.)_

### fti_update_servers_xform
The other exception in `Camera3D` is that it *does* implement `fti_update_servers_xform()`, because the camera uses some non-standard synchronization / calculations in `_get_adjusted_camera_transform()` if I remember right.

